1
00:00:04,733 --> 00:00:11,733
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:32,700
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:34,867
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:41,200
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,067 --> 00:00:43,700
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:44,967
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:46,067
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:48,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:51,033
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:53,467
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,300
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,467 --> 00:00:57,867
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,233
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,867 --> 00:01:03,033
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,067 --> 00:01:06,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:09,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,033 --> 00:01:11,567
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:12,800
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,933 --> 00:01:14,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:20,833
<i> Something fell from above.</i>

21
00:01:20,967 --> 00:01:23,500
<i>She was shot.
Her life is clearly in danger.</i>

22
00:01:23,633 --> 00:01:25,767
<i>Don't tell anyone,
not even our neighbors.</i>

23
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:27,000
<i> Samantha was ambushed.</i>

24
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:28,867
<i>You're the only one who can
do this to my daughter!</i>

25
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,267
<i>How many times
do I have to tell you this?</i>

26
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:33,167
<i> Your daughter isn't here!</i>

27
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:36,267
If anything happens to Samantha,
<i> I'll come back for you.</i>

28
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:38,567
<i>We'll be right here
waiting for you.</i>

29
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:39,633
<i> This is your fault!</i>

30
00:01:39,767 --> 00:01:41,167
<i>You failed to protect
my daughter!</i>

31
00:01:41,333 --> 00:01:43,667
<i>Finding her is
the NCIA's top priority.</i>

32
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:45,933
<i>They could blow up
this entire NCIA</i>

33
00:01:46,067 --> 00:01:47,233
<i> just to get Victor out!</i>

34
00:01:47,367 --> 00:01:48,433
<i> So I'm telling you now</i>

35
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:50,233
<i>to transfer him
to maximum security.</i>

36
00:01:50,367 --> 00:01:52,300
<i> Is Gabo doing the right thing?</i>

37
00:01:52,433 --> 00:01:53,967
<i>Who are you?
What's your name?!</i>

38
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:55,067
<i> Don't point that gun!</i>

39
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,767
<i>Don't! You might fire it!
Calm down, miss!</i>

40
00:01:57,900 --> 00:01:59,233
<i> We'll explain everything.</i>

41
00:01:59,367 --> 00:02:03,000
<i>I need to pretend for now
so they won't make me leave.</i>

42
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:06,933
[GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]

43
00:02:07,067 --> 00:02:08,167
Who am I?!

44
00:02:08,867 --> 00:02:11,033
Rudy. Rudy, I think...

45
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:15,733
I think she hit her head
when she fell.

46
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:17,033
Yeah.

47
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,867
We'll talk about that later.
Put the gun down first!

48
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,033
[GABO]
<i> She's not in her right mind!</i>

49
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,467
What did you do to me?
Why am I here?

50
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,033
[GABO]<i> I need to pretend
</i> so she won't leave this place.

51
00:02:27,167 --> 00:02:30,167
<i>Otherwise,
her life would be in danger.</i>

52
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:33,000
- [GABO GRUNTING]
- Who are you?!

53
00:02:34,533 --> 00:02:36,933
[GABO GRUNTING]

54
00:02:37,067 --> 00:02:38,300
Honey!

55
00:02:38,433 --> 00:02:39,333
[GROANS]

56
00:02:39,467 --> 00:02:43,733
[SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

57
00:02:43,867 --> 00:02:45,133
You're Gloria!

58
00:02:46,067 --> 00:02:47,567
I'm your husband Gabo!

59
00:02:51,833 --> 00:02:53,333
[WHISPERING] Gloria?

60
00:02:53,467 --> 00:02:54,900
- [MOUTHS]<i> I don't know!
</i>- Honey!

61
00:02:55,033 --> 00:02:56,733
Drop the gun, you might fire it!

62
00:02:56,867 --> 00:02:59,033
[GABO GRUNTING]

63
00:02:59,167 --> 00:03:00,967
Husband?

64
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,000
No.

65
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:03,667
Y-You're my husband?

66
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:04,867
[SAM STAMMERING]

67
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,533
[KNOCKING ON WALL]

68
00:03:06,667 --> 00:03:10,233
I said keep quiet, you bastards!

69
00:03:12,033 --> 00:03:12,967
Sleep...

70
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:16,267
- Shh!
- Gloria,

71
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,633
I'll explain everything.

72
00:03:17,767 --> 00:03:19,567
[GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]

73
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,133
You were in an accident
last night.

74
00:03:22,033 --> 00:03:26,500
You fell from the roof,
and hit your head.

75
00:03:26,633 --> 00:03:28,800
That's why
you can't remember anything.

76
00:03:29,667 --> 00:03:32,667
So you better drop the gun!
It might go off!

77
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:34,067
You're going to kill me, honey!

78
00:03:34,633 --> 00:03:36,200
- [GABO GRUNTING]
- [MAMENG] Come on, miss.

79
00:03:36,333 --> 00:03:39,000
No! I don't--
I don't remember anything.

80
00:03:39,567 --> 00:03:42,200
Honey, please.

81
00:03:42,733 --> 00:03:43,900
Believe me.

82
00:03:45,033 --> 00:03:46,533
I am your husband Gabo.

83
00:03:46,667 --> 00:03:47,733
[GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]

84
00:03:47,867 --> 00:03:50,433
Gloria, drop the gun.

85
00:03:50,567 --> 00:03:53,600
That might go off.
I'm going to die!

86
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,200
[GABO GROANS]

87
00:03:55,367 --> 00:03:59,167
H-Husband-- I don't--
I don't remember at all.

88
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:02,533
I'll explain everything.
Just drop the gun first.

89
00:04:02,667 --> 00:04:05,600
- Come on. I'm begging you.
- [MAMENG] Put it down.

90
00:04:05,733 --> 00:04:07,933
[GABO GRUNTING]

91
00:04:08,067 --> 00:04:09,167
Drop it.

92
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,733
- Drop it.
- No!

93
00:04:10,867 --> 00:04:13,200
I'll explain everything
to you, Gloria.

94
00:04:13,333 --> 00:04:14,567
Drop it.

95
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:18,867
[GABO SIGHS IN RELIEF,
BREATHING HEAVILY]

96
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
[SAM] Who am I? Wait.

97
00:04:21,733 --> 00:04:24,500
I don't remember who I am!

98
00:04:25,067 --> 00:04:28,967
[GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]

99
00:04:33,833 --> 00:04:34,900
[GABO STAMMERING]

100
00:04:35,033 --> 00:04:36,933
I-I know
you don't remember anything.

101
00:04:37,967 --> 00:04:39,733
But let me explain everything
to you.

102
00:04:39,867 --> 00:04:42,500
- [SAM WHIMPERING]
- [GABO BREATHING HEAVILY]

103
00:04:42,633 --> 00:04:43,733
Don't be afraid.

104
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:45,567
I'm your husband.

105
00:04:47,267 --> 00:04:48,667
I-I'm not going to hurt you.

106
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:55,800
[SILLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

107
00:04:56,900 --> 00:04:58,100
It'd be better...

108
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:00,867
...for us to stay
in the kitchen.

109
00:05:01,033 --> 00:05:02,567
I'll explain everything
to you.

110
00:05:05,067 --> 00:05:07,300
- There's coffee there. Yes.
- Yes.

111
00:05:07,433 --> 00:05:09,467
[MAMENG] Come on.
Just relax, okay?

112
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:12,400
- [RUDY] Come.
- [MAMENG] Just relax, dear.

113
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:15,400
I don't remember anything
at all.

114
00:05:15,533 --> 00:05:16,833
[KNOCKING ON WALL]

115
00:05:16,967 --> 00:05:18,867
- Shh! Shh!
- [BETCHAY] What's with you?

116
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,067
Really?

117
00:05:20,733 --> 00:05:22,667
One, two, three!

118
00:05:23,867 --> 00:05:25,333
Your dad's bald.

119
00:05:25,467 --> 00:05:27,433
Come, come, come. Come.

120
00:05:29,133 --> 00:05:32,033
- She has that thing.
- What thing? Walk slowly.

121
00:05:32,167 --> 00:05:34,300
[MAMENG] That illness
where you lose your memories.

122
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:35,667
Ah, yeah! Like kali.

123
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,900
- What's "kali"?
<i> - Kalimot (forget)!</i>

124
00:05:38,033 --> 00:05:39,900
- Amnesia!
- Oh, yeah! Exactly!

125
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:45,867
[SILLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

126
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,933
- You should eat.
- [CHAIR SCRAPING]

127
00:05:50,467 --> 00:05:51,433
Are you alright?

128
00:05:52,733 --> 00:05:55,733
Wait, if you're my husband...

129
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:58,900
Are you really my husband?

130
00:05:59,033 --> 00:06:01,267
[GASPS] Husband?!
Did she say "husband"?!

131
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:02,900
- [BONG] She did. Yeah.
- Yeah?

132
00:06:03,033 --> 00:06:06,833
[SILLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

133
00:06:06,967 --> 00:06:08,133
Honey...

134
00:06:09,267 --> 00:06:10,300
Gloria...

135
00:06:11,233 --> 00:06:12,233
Honey.

136
00:06:13,433 --> 00:06:14,900
I'm your husband Gabo!

137
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:18,700
I know
you don't remember anything.

138
00:06:20,133 --> 00:06:23,667
It's 'cause you hit your head
last night, but...

139
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:24,867
Don't worry.

140
00:06:25,433 --> 00:06:26,933
I'll help
you remember everything.

141
00:06:27,533 --> 00:06:31,367
[GABO BREATHING DEEPLY]

142
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:32,567
[OBJECT CREAKS]

143
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:34,333
What about my wound?

144
00:06:39,067 --> 00:06:40,367
[GABO STAMMERING]

145
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,633
Honey, I got confused, too.

146
00:06:44,367 --> 00:06:47,967
When you came back last night,
I was surprised to see...

147
00:06:48,667 --> 00:06:50,900
You've got a bullet in your arm.

148
00:06:51,867 --> 00:06:54,733
You told me there are men
after you.

149
00:06:55,367 --> 00:06:58,333
I was surprised
'cause you had a gun!

150
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,200
You really don't
remember anything?

151
00:07:03,333 --> 00:07:04,267
Nothing.

152
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:06,767
I don't remember anything.

153
00:07:08,133 --> 00:07:11,733
Uh, dear, let's not make
too much noise.

154
00:07:11,867 --> 00:07:15,533
We live with someone
who's very grumpy!

155
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,733
And we can't wake her.

156
00:07:18,167 --> 00:07:19,133
Uh...

157
00:07:19,767 --> 00:07:24,267
If I'm your wife,
do we have kids?

158
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:26,667
Uhh...

159
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,333
[GABO CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

160
00:07:31,467 --> 00:07:37,433
Uh, honey, we've been planning
for it for a long time.

161
00:07:37,567 --> 00:07:39,367
We've tried...

162
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:43,067
to have kids many times...

163
00:07:44,167 --> 00:07:45,900
...but God hasn't blessed us
with any yet.

164
00:07:46,033 --> 00:07:47,133
[GABO CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

165
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,333
But, honey, don't worry.

166
00:07:49,967 --> 00:07:51,000
Tonight...

167
00:07:54,533 --> 00:07:56,900
- We'll make a baby.
- [RUDY COUGHS]

168
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:04,033
- That woman's dead to me!
- Tekla, wait!

169
00:08:04,167 --> 00:08:05,367
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

170
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:06,767
[TOLITS] Why are you
in such a hurry?!

171
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:09,033
- What's with you, Tekla?!
- What are you talking about?

172
00:08:09,167 --> 00:08:10,467
What "husband"
are you talking about?

173
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:12,433
- What's with you?!
- [GABO] Uhh...

174
00:08:12,567 --> 00:08:13,567
[TEKLA] That's your wife?

175
00:08:14,167 --> 00:08:15,100
Uhh...

176
00:08:15,233 --> 00:08:16,067
Yeah!

177
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:17,533
- [TEKLA GASPS]
- Gloria!

178
00:08:17,667 --> 00:08:19,533
What are you talking about?!
What's with you?!

179
00:08:19,667 --> 00:08:21,667
Wake up, Gabo!

180
00:08:21,833 --> 00:08:23,933
Sir Rudy, do something
about your son!

181
00:08:24,067 --> 00:08:25,033
- Hey, Tekla.
- What's with you?!

182
00:08:25,167 --> 00:08:29,300
Gloria and I
were talking about...

183
00:08:31,733 --> 00:08:33,033
We're going to make
a baby tonight.

184
00:08:33,167 --> 00:08:35,600
- Ahh! Ah! [CRYING]
- Ah!

185
00:08:35,733 --> 00:08:37,933
Why is there suddenly a baby?!

186
00:08:38,067 --> 00:08:41,333
You didn't tell us about that!
Gabo, what's with you?!

187
00:08:41,467 --> 00:08:43,467
- [RUDY] Hey, Tekla! Stop.
- What are you talking about?!

188
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,833
That's enough.

189
00:08:44,967 --> 00:08:46,200
You won't get anything
anymore from Gabo

190
00:08:46,333 --> 00:08:48,333
because he has a wife
and a family now!

191
00:08:48,467 --> 00:08:50,900
- Right? Right?
- Uh, y-yes! Yes!

192
00:08:51,033 --> 00:08:52,933
- [TEKLA CRYING]
- [MAMENG] And, Tekla,

193
00:08:53,067 --> 00:08:56,533
stop troubling Gabo and, uh--

194
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:58,767
- Gloria.
- Gloria!

195
00:08:58,900 --> 00:09:00,767
Their lives are now peaceful!

196
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:02,967
[TEKLA CRYING] No, Miss Mameng!

197
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:06,100
I know you know!
Gabo, why?!

198
00:09:06,233 --> 00:09:07,600
- What's with you?!
- Tekla, that's enough!

199
00:09:07,733 --> 00:09:10,333
- That's enough, that's enough.
- [MUFFLED SCREAMING]

200
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:11,633
- Let's go!
- We're sorry.

201
00:09:11,767 --> 00:09:12,867
- [MUFFLED SCREAMING]
- She's heavy!

202
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,633
- She thinks she's all that.
- [BINOY] She's heavy!

203
00:09:14,767 --> 00:09:16,933
- Wait, she's heavy!
- [MUFFLED SCREAMING]

204
00:09:17,067 --> 00:09:18,500
[SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

205
00:09:18,633 --> 00:09:20,800
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

206
00:09:20,933 --> 00:09:22,500
- Why did you stop me?!
- Shh, shh!

207
00:09:22,633 --> 00:09:23,833
- I'm mad!
- Shh!

208
00:09:23,967 --> 00:09:25,533
Don't shush me!

209
00:09:25,667 --> 00:09:27,667
Why did you go along with it?!
I don't understand!

210
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:31,367
Explain to me why Sir Rudy
and Miss Mameng

211
00:09:31,533 --> 00:09:33,900
are saying she's Gabo's wife!
She's not his wife!

212
00:09:34,033 --> 00:09:35,333
Didn't she just fall
through the roof?!

213
00:09:35,467 --> 00:09:37,467
Tekla! Stop it!

214
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:41,067
Don't you get it?
Gabo was just pretending.

215
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:43,533
- Pretending?
- So Sir Rudy and Miss Mameng

216
00:09:43,667 --> 00:09:45,100
are pretending, too!

217
00:09:45,233 --> 00:09:48,433
No! Well, why do they need
to pretend?!

218
00:09:48,567 --> 00:09:50,633
Honey, I'm sorry.

219
00:09:50,767 --> 00:09:53,700
She's a bit nuts.

220
00:09:53,833 --> 00:09:56,633
[SAM] Who is she?
Why was she causing a scene?

221
00:09:56,767 --> 00:09:59,600
That woman is Tekla!

222
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:02,600
She's been with Gabo
since childhood, right?

223
00:10:02,767 --> 00:10:03,733
Mm-hmm.

224
00:10:04,567 --> 00:10:07,133
She's head over heels for him.

225
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:09,700
[GABO CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

226
00:10:09,833 --> 00:10:13,033
Honey, don't worry.
Nothing wrong's going on.

227
00:10:14,433 --> 00:10:15,833
You are the only one I love.

228
00:10:15,967 --> 00:10:18,733
[SILLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

229
00:10:18,867 --> 00:10:21,033
And I made that promise
for eternity.

230
00:10:23,533 --> 00:10:25,200
[SAM] This guy's shameless.

231
00:10:25,767 --> 00:10:26,933
<i> He's such a smooth-talker!</i>

232
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,867
<i> Does he think he's handsome?</i>

233
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,800
<i> Hey! I won't ever like you!</i>

234
00:10:32,933 --> 00:10:35,600
[SILLY MUSIC CONTINUES]

235
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:39,533
[DOOR SLIDES]

236
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:43,600
Um, sir, this is the printout
of the court order

237
00:10:43,733 --> 00:10:47,033
- for Victor Zafra's transfer.
- Okay, let me see.

238
00:10:47,167 --> 00:10:48,233
Okay, thank you.

239
00:10:51,967 --> 00:10:53,167
[DELGADO SIGHS DEEPLY]

240
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:54,767
- [DELGADO] Team.
- [DOCUMENT THUDS]

241
00:10:55,333 --> 00:10:58,500
We've received the court order
for Victor Zafra's transfer

242
00:10:58,633 --> 00:11:01,300
to the maximum security
detention facility.

243
00:11:01,433 --> 00:11:03,933
[CASTOR] But, sir,
we haven't filed a case yet.

244
00:11:04,067 --> 00:11:06,367
[DELGADO] That's because
of what happened to Mr. Chan.

245
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:10,067
And the possible connection
to Sam's ambush.

246
00:11:10,233 --> 00:11:12,167
To cancel out all assumptions...

247
00:11:12,733 --> 00:11:16,000
Did General Jacinto order this?

248
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:17,100
Yes.

249
00:11:17,233 --> 00:11:20,400
He's questioning
the NCIA's capabilities.

250
00:11:20,533 --> 00:11:23,933
We have to prove to him
that we can find solid evidence

251
00:11:24,067 --> 00:11:26,233
- against the Zafras!
- [SEBASTIAN] Sir, don't worry.

252
00:11:26,367 --> 00:11:28,967
Tiger is safe with us.
We'll transfer him ourselves.

253
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:31,167
Sir, we'll join the escort.

254
00:11:31,300 --> 00:11:32,233
- Right, team?
- Yes.

255
00:11:32,367 --> 00:11:33,433
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, I know

256
00:11:33,567 --> 00:11:35,567
you're all worried about Sam.

257
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:38,767
However, we still have
a lot of work to do.

258
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:40,333
Sir, while we're doing that,

259
00:11:40,467 --> 00:11:44,633
we'll assign agents
to continue searching for Sam.

260
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:46,133
That's good.

261
00:11:46,267 --> 00:11:50,033
For now, prepare
to transfer Victor Zafra.

262
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:51,900
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

263
00:11:53,167 --> 00:11:54,967
Sir. Ma'am.

264
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:56,933
Attorney and I
just finished talking.

265
00:11:57,067 --> 00:11:58,400
He said Victor's
being transferred

266
00:11:58,533 --> 00:12:00,533
to a maximum security
detention facility.

267
00:12:00,667 --> 00:12:02,467
Once Victor's transferred...

268
00:12:03,233 --> 00:12:05,267
...it'll be harder
to get him out.

269
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:08,033
We can take this
as a blessing in disguise.

270
00:12:08,167 --> 00:12:12,033
If they move Victor
from the NCIA,

271
00:12:12,167 --> 00:12:16,967
we'll have a chance
to intercept their convoy,

272
00:12:17,133 --> 00:12:18,967
and we can get him out.

273
00:12:21,467 --> 00:12:24,600
[PHONE RINGING]

274
00:12:24,733 --> 00:12:26,233
Double check everything.

275
00:12:27,133 --> 00:12:29,233
- Colonel Domingo.
- [DOMINGO] General Jacinto!

276
00:12:29,367 --> 00:12:31,933
We're focusing
on looking for Samantha.

277
00:12:32,067 --> 00:12:35,400
Okay. Later, the NCIA
will transfer Victor Zafra

278
00:12:35,533 --> 00:12:36,700
to maximum security.

279
00:12:36,833 --> 00:12:38,267
[RICARDO]<i> There's no denying
</i> he had something to do

280
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,767
<i>with what happened
to my daughter.</i>

281
00:12:39,900 --> 00:12:41,633
I want you to be part
of that transfer.

282
00:12:41,767 --> 00:12:46,000
General, the NCIA is keeping us
from doing our job properly.

283
00:12:46,133 --> 00:12:48,200
<i>- They might prohibit me.
- That's my point.</i>

284
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:50,733
I don't trust the NCIA.

285
00:12:50,867 --> 00:12:52,867
<i> - I'm counting on you.
</i>- Yes, General Jacinto.

286
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,200
You can count on us.

287
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:56,033
Umali.

288
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:57,833
Bring some men.

289
00:12:57,967 --> 00:13:00,433
You have to go
to the NCIA right now.

290
00:13:00,567 --> 00:13:01,767
Again, sir? Why?

291
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:05,300
Victor Zafra's being transferred
to a maximum security facility.

292
00:13:05,433 --> 00:13:09,433
General Jacinto wants us
to escort him.

293
00:13:10,233 --> 00:13:11,767
He has no trust in the NCIA.

294
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:14,933
He really shouldn't trust
those bastards.

295
00:13:15,067 --> 00:13:16,567
What are you waiting for?
Let's go!

296
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:17,833
Yes, sir!

297
00:13:19,133 --> 00:13:21,133
Wait, didn't you notice?

298
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,867
I think there's something wrong
with that woman.

299
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,533
She doesn't seem to be okay.
Don't you think she has--

300
00:13:25,667 --> 00:13:27,600
- Maybe she has amnesia!
- [BINOY GASPS]

301
00:13:27,733 --> 00:13:30,900
Amnesia?! So that's why
she doesn't remember anything.

302
00:13:31,033 --> 00:13:32,100
[TOLITS SLAMS TABLE]

303
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:34,967
Gabo's pretending
to be the husband

304
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:37,500
- of that female NCIA agent.
- But wait.

305
00:13:37,633 --> 00:13:40,333
What if she finds out
Gabo's only pretending?

306
00:13:40,467 --> 00:13:41,800
We'll have to plan for that.

307
00:13:41,933 --> 00:13:44,867
For now, let's leave them be.

308
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,167
Otherwise,
we might ruin their plans!

309
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:50,367
No, no! What do you mean,
"leave them be"? We won't!

310
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:51,900
I don't care what happens.

311
00:13:52,033 --> 00:13:55,867
I won't join you in pretending.
Do it if you want! I won't!

312
00:13:56,033 --> 00:13:58,467
- Keep quiet! They can hear you!
- I don't care!

313
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:02,300
[MAMENG] Gabo, I think
we should let her eat.

314
00:14:02,433 --> 00:14:05,633
Didn't Betchay bring home
some pansit?

315
00:14:05,767 --> 00:14:07,000
We left it outside.
It might go bad.

316
00:14:07,133 --> 00:14:09,200
- Go get it.
- [RUDY] Get it, Gabo. Go.

317
00:14:09,333 --> 00:14:11,500
Honey, I'll just get
the pansit.

318
00:14:11,633 --> 00:14:12,700
- Stay here.
- [MAMENG] Yes.

319
00:14:12,833 --> 00:14:14,300
[GABO] I'll just get it.

320
00:14:14,433 --> 00:14:15,433
[PLATES CLATTERING]

321
00:14:15,567 --> 00:14:16,533
[MAMENG] Look.

322
00:14:16,667 --> 00:14:18,000
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

323
00:14:18,133 --> 00:14:19,400
[MAMENG] Oh, there we go.

324
00:14:19,533 --> 00:14:21,633
Do you like dried herring, dear?

325
00:14:22,133 --> 00:14:24,233
[SAM] You think you can fool me?

326
00:14:24,933 --> 00:14:26,333
<i> What you don't know...</i>

327
00:14:26,467 --> 00:14:29,100
<i>is that I'm the one
pulling the strings.</i>

328
00:14:30,067 --> 00:14:34,033
<i>I'll find out your connection
to Zafra and Mr. Chan.</i>

329
00:14:34,567 --> 00:14:38,467
<i>And all of you will end up
behind bars together.</i>

330
00:14:39,767 --> 00:14:40,833
Gabo, what was that?!

331
00:14:40,967 --> 00:14:41,833
- Hey, hey!
- Shh!

332
00:14:41,967 --> 00:14:42,833
[MUFFLED SPEAKING]

333
00:14:42,967 --> 00:14:43,933
Not too loud!

334
00:14:44,067 --> 00:14:44,867
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

335
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:45,867
[GRUNTS]

336
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,433
What the heck
did you say earlier?

337
00:14:47,567 --> 00:14:48,733
She's not your wife, is she?

338
00:14:48,867 --> 00:14:50,633
Then why did you tell her
otherwise?

339
00:14:50,767 --> 00:14:51,667
Tekla!

340
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:52,667
[TEKLA BREATHES HEAVILY]

341
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:53,733
Calm down!

342
00:14:53,867 --> 00:14:55,133
[SIGHS EXASPERATEDLY]

343
00:14:58,067 --> 00:14:59,267
We've got a problem.

344
00:14:59,567 --> 00:15:01,133
That woman fell into our house.

345
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:03,933
When she woke up,
she couldn't remember a thing.

346
00:15:04,833 --> 00:15:06,900
That means she's got amnesia.

347
00:15:07,033 --> 00:15:08,667
- So we need to pretend.
- I knew it!

348
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:10,067
Well, no!

349
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,967
I don't care
what happens to her!

350
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:14,200
Amnesia, seriously?

351
00:15:14,333 --> 00:15:15,267
She's being so dramatic!

352
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:16,300
[GABO] Tekla.

353
00:15:16,433 --> 00:15:18,200
We need to help her.

354
00:15:18,333 --> 00:15:19,200
[HUFFS]

355
00:15:19,333 --> 00:15:21,067
Because once
that woman finds out

356
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,667
none of what
we're telling is true,

357
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:23,900
she'll leave for sure!

358
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:26,567
Her enemies are waiting outside

359
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:27,833
and they'll kill her!

360
00:15:27,967 --> 00:15:30,167
Oh, she can leave if she wants!
I don't give a damn, Gabo!

361
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:33,767
What I don't understand is why
she has to stay in your house!

362
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:35,467
She could've stayed
anywhere else!

363
00:15:35,633 --> 00:15:36,833
- His house! Or even mine!
- Why my house?

364
00:15:36,967 --> 00:15:37,867
Let her stay with us instead!

365
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,000
She can stay in my room,
but not in your house

366
00:15:40,133 --> 00:15:41,500
and definitely not in your room!

367
00:15:41,633 --> 00:15:43,333
[INHALES DEEPLY, SIGHS]

368
00:15:43,833 --> 00:15:45,333
It's too late for that.

369
00:15:46,433 --> 00:15:47,633
What's done is done,

370
00:15:47,767 --> 00:15:49,333
and now we have to play along.

371
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:53,767
All she knows is
that I'm her husband.

372
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:54,767
[MUMBLING]

373
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:56,467
And she is my wife.

374
00:15:56,833 --> 00:15:58,700
Her name is Gloria.

375
00:15:58,833 --> 00:15:59,767
Got it?

376
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:01,200
[MUMBLING]

377
00:16:01,900 --> 00:16:02,933
Just let it go, Tekla.

378
00:16:03,067 --> 00:16:04,233
As soon as her memories return,

379
00:16:04,367 --> 00:16:05,467
the truth will surely come out.

380
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:08,933
Gabo is only doing all of this
to protect her.

381
00:16:09,100 --> 00:16:10,467
If that happened to you,

382
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:12,267
Gabo would do the same thing.

383
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:14,300
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

384
00:16:14,433 --> 00:16:15,400
Really?

385
00:16:15,533 --> 00:16:16,700
[BINOY SNICKERS]

386
00:16:16,833 --> 00:16:18,567
You'd do the same for me?

387
00:16:22,233 --> 00:16:23,300
Tekla...

388
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:25,467
Ever since we were kids,

389
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:27,200
you know

390
00:16:27,333 --> 00:16:28,667
how I've always made sure
to take care of you

391
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:29,700
and protect you.

392
00:16:29,833 --> 00:16:31,800
I won't let you
get even a scratch.

393
00:16:31,933 --> 00:16:33,900
I'm willing to put my life
on the line for you.

394
00:16:34,033 --> 00:16:35,067
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

395
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,067
[SQUEALS]

396
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,700
So that settles it then.
Okay, you got me.

397
00:16:37,833 --> 00:16:39,000
- I'm fine now.
- Whoa, whoa!

398
00:16:39,133 --> 00:16:40,700
- You went soft just like that?
- She folded real quick.

399
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:42,567
- Such a flirt!
- Stop it!

400
00:16:42,733 --> 00:16:43,733
What a killjoy.

401
00:16:43,867 --> 00:16:45,533
You keep ruining things for me.

402
00:16:45,667 --> 00:16:47,033
Now, listen up.

403
00:16:47,733 --> 00:16:49,000
If possible,

404
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:50,900
no one else should know
about this.

405
00:16:51,933 --> 00:16:54,433
Only we know who she really is.

406
00:16:54,867 --> 00:16:56,167
- Yes, Gabo!
- Yes, Gabo!

407
00:16:56,300 --> 00:16:57,267
Fine.

408
00:16:57,400 --> 00:17:04,367
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

409
00:17:10,167 --> 00:17:12,067
You won't tell anyone, okay?

410
00:17:12,467 --> 00:17:14,300
- Yeah.
- Damn right, Gabo.

411
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:16,200
He brought food. Looks like
it's their anniversary.

412
00:17:16,233 --> 00:17:18,067
- Please put it there.
- Sure thing.

413
00:17:18,467 --> 00:17:19,933
[MAMENG] Oh, he's back!

414
00:17:19,933 --> 00:17:21,167
- [RUDY] The food's here.
- Love.

415
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,867
[GABO] Here come the noodles.

416
00:17:23,867 --> 00:17:25,167
- Let me unwrap it.
- Okay.

417
00:17:25,167 --> 00:17:28,233
- This is so good.
- [RUDY] That's right.

418
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:29,600
Gabo.

419
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:31,500
How did you two meet?

420
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:32,533
[GABO] Pa...

421
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:35,000
It's a... It's a long story.

422
00:17:35,433 --> 00:17:37,433
Maybe I'll tell you about it
another day.

423
00:17:37,433 --> 00:17:38,700
[RUDY] Ah.

424
00:17:38,933 --> 00:17:44,133
[MAMENG] You didn't even tell us
that you got married already.

425
00:17:44,133 --> 00:17:45,267
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

426
00:17:45,267 --> 00:17:46,400
[GABO] I'm sorry, Auntie.

427
00:17:47,067 --> 00:17:48,967
I've been really busy.

428
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,900
- Mm-hmm.
- Plus...

429
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:55,200
I'm too shy to tell you
the story.

430
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:58,167
Maybe we should
serve her food now.

431
00:17:58,167 --> 00:17:59,500
She's starving already.

432
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:00,633
- Of course.
- Yes.

433
00:18:00,633 --> 00:18:02,000
[MAMENG] Let's give her some.

434
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:03,167
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

435
00:18:03,167 --> 00:18:04,333
So, Gina...

436
00:18:04,933 --> 00:18:06,000
Gloria.

437
00:18:07,767 --> 00:18:09,200
[MAMENG] Gloria...

438
00:18:09,767 --> 00:18:13,267
Well, do you truly
not remember anything?

439
00:18:16,333 --> 00:18:17,400
Uh...

440
00:18:17,900 --> 00:18:20,533
Oh, I'm so sorry. I don't really
remember anything.

441
00:18:21,333 --> 00:18:23,267
[MAMENG] Oh, don't worry.

442
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:25,333
While you're here,

443
00:18:25,333 --> 00:18:27,467
we'll take care of you.

444
00:18:27,467 --> 00:18:28,600
[RUDY] Right.

445
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:29,767
And if you need anything,

446
00:18:29,767 --> 00:18:31,633
just tell me and Mameng.

447
00:18:31,633 --> 00:18:32,700
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

448
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:34,133
[RUDY] Gabo, I'll just
step out for a bit

449
00:18:34,133 --> 00:18:35,967
and see how
the car repair is going.

450
00:18:35,967 --> 00:18:37,933
- Enjoy your meal.
- Give her more noodles.

451
00:18:38,767 --> 00:18:39,900
[GABO] Dig in, love.

452
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,833
[DANTE] The spark plug needs
to be replaced.

453
00:18:43,833 --> 00:18:45,033
[ELTON] Replace the spark plug.

454
00:18:45,033 --> 00:18:48,767
The distributor's faulty, too.

455
00:18:48,767 --> 00:18:49,967
- Hey, Rudy.
- Hmm?

456
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:52,833
Look, I couldn't help
but notice...

457
00:18:52,833 --> 00:18:54,967
What's causing all the chaos
in your house?

458
00:18:55,367 --> 00:18:56,933
- What?
- Is it because of Betchay?

459
00:18:57,367 --> 00:18:58,433
No.

460
00:18:58,433 --> 00:18:59,700
No, no.

461
00:18:59,700 --> 00:19:02,467
Gabo's wife just arrived.

462
00:19:02,467 --> 00:19:03,767
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

463
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:04,800
What?

464
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:05,933
[SIGHS]

465
00:19:06,233 --> 00:19:07,433
- [ELTON] Rudy.
- Hmm?

466
00:19:07,433 --> 00:19:09,500
Is what you said true?
Gabo is already married?

467
00:19:10,033 --> 00:19:12,100
She came last night.

468
00:19:12,100 --> 00:19:14,367
Just like I said, she's inside.

469
00:19:14,367 --> 00:19:15,733
Gabo tied the knot already?

470
00:19:15,733 --> 00:19:17,433
Without even telling us?

471
00:19:17,433 --> 00:19:20,700
[ELTON] He didn't mention
about a wedding at all.

472
00:19:26,067 --> 00:19:27,100
[MUSIC ENDS]

473
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:34,067
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

474
00:19:40,333 --> 00:19:41,800
[SIGHING]

475
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:47,067
[PHONE RINGING]

476
00:19:47,967 --> 00:19:49,200
Pia.

477
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:51,700
Victor's going to be transferred
to maximum security today.

478
00:19:51,700 --> 00:19:52,833
Today?

479
00:19:52,833 --> 00:19:54,500
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

480
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:55,967
Alright, we'll start
our preparations.

481
00:19:55,967 --> 00:19:57,667
You need to move fast.

482
00:19:57,667 --> 00:19:59,300
There'll be plenty of escorts.

483
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:01,800
Damn it!

484
00:20:01,800 --> 00:20:02,900
[INHALES DEEPLY]

485
00:20:02,933 --> 00:20:04,133
Alright.

486
00:20:04,133 --> 00:20:06,133
Signal Victor when it's time.

487
00:20:06,533 --> 00:20:07,667
O-Okay, okay.

488
00:20:07,667 --> 00:20:08,967
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

489
00:20:08,967 --> 00:20:10,200
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

490
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:11,633
[DEBORAH] I know...

491
00:20:11,633 --> 00:20:14,700
the exact route
Victor will be taking.

492
00:20:15,733 --> 00:20:17,067
- Arturo.
- Sir?

493
00:20:17,067 --> 00:20:18,800
- Get the men ready.
- Yes, sir.

494
00:20:18,800 --> 00:20:19,933
[GUN COCKING]

495
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:25,233
This is our best chance.

496
00:20:25,233 --> 00:20:28,500
If we don't break him out today,

497
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:32,700
we're going to have a hard time
finding another chance

498
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:34,100
to do it.

499
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,200
I know.

500
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:38,533
I'll bring your son home later.

501
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,633
[SLIDING DOORS OPEN]

502
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:47,500
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

503
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:49,500
[LAWYER]
The NCIA will transfer you

504
00:20:49,500 --> 00:20:51,400
to another detention
center today.

505
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:52,767
Wait, where?

506
00:20:53,167 --> 00:20:54,267
To...

507
00:20:54,633 --> 00:20:57,567
a maximum security
detention facility.

508
00:20:57,567 --> 00:20:58,700
Why?

509
00:20:58,700 --> 00:21:02,400
Because of what happened
to Mr. Chan and Sam Jacinto,

510
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:04,733
the court believes that
you are a high-risk detainee.

511
00:21:04,733 --> 00:21:10,367
Security and the investigation
might be compromised

512
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,567
while you are here.

513
00:21:11,567 --> 00:21:15,233
They haven't even charged me
with anything!

514
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:17,267
This is only temporary

515
00:21:17,267 --> 00:21:19,933
while the investigation
is ongoing.

516
00:21:19,933 --> 00:21:21,933
And you just let it happen?

517
00:21:21,933 --> 00:21:23,633
You didn't do anything!

518
00:21:23,633 --> 00:21:25,367
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

519
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:27,233
You're useless!

520
00:21:27,233 --> 00:21:28,367
We are going to--

521
00:21:28,367 --> 00:21:29,967
- We are going to appeal!
- Guard!

522
00:21:30,233 --> 00:21:34,600
However, you are required
to comply with all court orders!

523
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:36,333
[VICTOR] You're getting paid
a lot of money,

524
00:21:36,333 --> 00:21:38,367
yet you did nothing to stop it!

525
00:21:38,767 --> 00:21:40,967
- Moron!
- That's enough!

526
00:21:40,967 --> 00:21:47,967
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

527
00:21:49,033 --> 00:21:50,200
Zafra.

528
00:21:51,467 --> 00:21:52,733
Wait a minute.

529
00:21:54,933 --> 00:21:56,533
Here is the court order.

530
00:21:56,900 --> 00:22:00,800
To make it clear that
your transfer process is legal.

531
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:03,833
Would you like to read it?

532
00:22:05,600 --> 00:22:06,533
Here.

533
00:22:06,933 --> 00:22:08,633
Read it.

534
00:22:11,133 --> 00:22:15,233
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

535
00:22:15,267 --> 00:22:16,667
Alright, take him inside.

536
00:22:23,533 --> 00:22:24,800
[KEYS JINGLE]

537
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:26,333
- [GATE SQUEAKS]
- [GATE HANDLE CLANKING]

538
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:29,833
"Your family will
break you out."

539
00:22:33,933 --> 00:22:35,767
By the way, Gabo,
once we finish eating,

540
00:22:36,567 --> 00:22:38,633
head to your room

541
00:22:38,767 --> 00:22:43,833
and get everything she needs
for bathing.

542
00:22:43,967 --> 00:22:46,500
Bring some clothes
for her to borrow.

543
00:22:46,633 --> 00:22:50,533
Also, prepare the medicine
for cleaning her wound.

544
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:52,067
[GABO] Y-Yes, Auntie.

545
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:53,300
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

546
00:22:53,433 --> 00:22:54,733
Love, try this.

547
00:22:55,933 --> 00:22:56,967
Here.

548
00:22:59,433 --> 00:23:00,400
Open your mouth.

549
00:23:01,667 --> 00:23:02,600
[GABO EXHALES]

550
00:23:02,733 --> 00:23:03,667
[BOTH CHUCKLE SOFTLY]

551
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:04,633
Yummy?

552
00:23:04,767 --> 00:23:05,800
Mm-hmm.
[GIGGLES]

553
00:23:05,933 --> 00:23:07,500
- [GABO BREATHES DEEPLY]
- [UTENSILS CLATTER]

554
00:23:07,633 --> 00:23:09,900
- Excuse me, Auntie.
- [MAMENG] Hmm?

555
00:23:10,033 --> 00:23:12,833
I'll just set up the room
and grab her some clothes

556
00:23:12,967 --> 00:23:15,200
so we can start fixing her up.

557
00:23:15,333 --> 00:23:16,900
[CHAIR RATTLING]

558
00:23:17,033 --> 00:23:18,100
Love you.

559
00:23:18,233 --> 00:23:22,533
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

560
00:23:22,700 --> 00:23:26,433
[FOOTSTEPS RECEDING]

561
00:23:28,333 --> 00:23:30,833
You know what?
Fine, let's just drink.

562
00:23:30,967 --> 00:23:31,800
- My treat.
- Whoa!

563
00:23:31,933 --> 00:23:33,000
- It's on me.
- You sure?

564
00:23:33,133 --> 00:23:34,233
- You're treating us?
- Totally.

565
00:23:34,367 --> 00:23:35,333
Take your seats.
Miss Simang!

566
00:23:35,467 --> 00:23:38,200
Bring us a case of beer
and some snacks!

567
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:40,133
- A whole case?
- Give them-- Yeah, why?

568
00:23:40,267 --> 00:23:42,000
Wow, Tekla, you get jealous
in such a big way!

569
00:23:42,133 --> 00:23:43,300
- Here's the case!
- A question!

570
00:23:43,433 --> 00:23:45,300
What more
if you were brokenhearted?

571
00:23:45,433 --> 00:23:47,767
You know what, Tekla?
I hope you'd always be jealous.

572
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:49,100
- Whoa!
- Grab your snacks!

573
00:23:49,233 --> 00:23:51,133
Is that what you want?
For me to feel bad?

574
00:23:51,267 --> 00:23:53,000
Not really.
You can't take a joke.

575
00:23:53,133 --> 00:23:55,400
[DABOY] Why force yourself
on Gabo anyway?

576
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:57,567
- I'm right here.
- Huh?

577
00:23:57,700 --> 00:23:59,467
Our breath smells the same.

578
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:00,667
- [HUFFING]
- Oh, wow.

579
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:02,833
Yours smells like acid.

580
00:24:02,967 --> 00:24:05,033
Look, I just can't accept it.

581
00:24:05,167 --> 00:24:07,467
Gabo and I have known
each other for a long time.

582
00:24:07,600 --> 00:24:10,133
We've been together
since we were kids.

583
00:24:10,233 --> 00:24:11,533
Enough of that, Tekla.

584
00:24:11,667 --> 00:24:14,167
You know how
you'll feel lighter?

585
00:24:14,300 --> 00:24:15,400
Just accept it.

586
00:24:15,533 --> 00:24:16,500
Accept it?

587
00:24:16,633 --> 00:24:18,400
You know, it's only
for a few days.

588
00:24:18,533 --> 00:24:19,867
Once Gloria recovers,

589
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,767
you'll have Gabo all
to yourself again.

590
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,167
- I hope so.
- Exactly.

591
00:24:23,300 --> 00:24:24,367
Hey, Tekla...

592
00:24:24,500 --> 00:24:30,567
[SILLY MUSIC PLAYING]

593
00:24:30,733 --> 00:24:32,533
I'm here if you don't want
Gabo anymore.

594
00:24:32,667 --> 00:24:33,767
Oh! [LAUGHS]

595
00:24:33,900 --> 00:24:35,967
- He's serious!
- Wow, he really is!

596
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:37,333
- You're serious, huh?
- Ouch!

597
00:24:37,467 --> 00:24:38,833
I can't take you seriously!

598
00:24:38,967 --> 00:24:39,833
You know what?

599
00:24:39,967 --> 00:24:43,400
Even if I black out
and crawl home drunk,

600
00:24:43,533 --> 00:24:44,933
I'd never go for you!

601
00:24:45,067 --> 00:24:45,900
- That hurts!
- [LAUGHS]

602
00:24:46,033 --> 00:24:48,100
And what you're saying...
[LAUGHS]

603
00:24:48,233 --> 00:24:49,767
You're nowhere near Gabo!

604
00:24:49,900 --> 00:24:51,067
So stay away from me!

605
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:52,433
Just have a drink.
Come on.

606
00:24:52,567 --> 00:24:54,233
Ask for the three bottles left.

607
00:24:54,367 --> 00:25:01,333
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

608
00:25:15,733 --> 00:25:22,133
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

609
00:25:22,267 --> 00:25:23,333
[DRAWER RATTLING]

610
00:25:30,367 --> 00:25:31,433
[BROOM RUSTLES]

611
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:42,133
[BROOM RUSTLING]

612
00:25:42,267 --> 00:25:49,267
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

613
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:57,333
[PILLOWS THUDDING]

614
00:26:02,900 --> 00:26:05,933
[MAMENG]
Oh, don't worry about it.

615
00:26:06,067 --> 00:26:07,167
Just get some rest, dear.

616
00:26:07,300 --> 00:26:09,633
By the way, how do you feel?

617
00:26:09,800 --> 00:26:10,633
Hmm?

618
00:26:10,767 --> 00:26:12,233
Uh, I'm fine.

619
00:26:12,367 --> 00:26:15,133
I'm just a little disoriented.

620
00:26:15,267 --> 00:26:16,700
Oh, well...

621
00:26:17,033 --> 00:26:20,967
With time, you'll start
feeling better.

622
00:26:21,333 --> 00:26:23,167
Can I ask you a question?

623
00:26:23,300 --> 00:26:24,467
Absolutely.

624
00:26:25,267 --> 00:26:27,567
About Gabo...
Where was he born?

625
00:26:27,700 --> 00:26:31,767
My nephew was born
in Mindoro.

626
00:26:31,900 --> 00:26:34,333
He's a very nice kid.

627
00:26:34,467 --> 00:26:36,400
And very hardworking, too.

628
00:26:36,533 --> 00:26:37,600
[MAMENG] And that's not all.

629
00:26:37,733 --> 00:26:41,533
He really cares
for the less unfortunate.

630
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:43,333
[SAM]
<i> That's the stolen motorcycle.</i>

631
00:26:43,467 --> 00:26:49,833
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

632
00:26:49,967 --> 00:26:51,967
<i> All my suspicious were right.</i>

633
00:26:53,167 --> 00:26:55,500
<i>I'll uncover who you
people really are</i>

634
00:26:55,633 --> 00:26:58,700
<i>and how you're linked
to Mr. Chan and the Zafras.</i>

635
00:26:59,867 --> 00:27:05,900
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

636
00:27:06,133 --> 00:27:08,900
<i>Victor Zafra is
a high-risk detainee,</i>

637
00:27:09,033 --> 00:27:11,767
<i>so let's assume the worst
during his transfer.</i>

638
00:27:11,900 --> 00:27:13,733
<i>- Bring back my son.
- I will.</i>

639
00:27:13,867 --> 00:27:17,133
<i>Unless you talk,
you'll waste away in prison.</i>

640
00:27:17,300 --> 00:27:18,333
<i> What's so funny?</i>

641
00:27:18,467 --> 00:27:20,000
<i>I'm just happy
about where I'm going.</i>

642
00:27:20,133 --> 00:27:22,433
<i> Join forces with your father.</i>

643
00:27:22,567 --> 00:27:24,233
<i>Together, you'll bring
Victor home.</i>

644
00:27:24,367 --> 00:27:26,233
<i> Victor Zafra is our priority.</i>

645
00:27:26,367 --> 00:27:27,333
<i> Whatever happens,</i>

646
00:27:27,467 --> 00:27:30,333
<i>we must take him
to maximum security detention.</i>

647
00:27:30,467 --> 00:27:31,833
<i>- Close in on them!
- Someone is following us!</i>

648
00:27:31,967 --> 00:27:32,833
<i> Cut them off now!</i>

649
00:27:32,967 --> 00:27:34,933
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [RAPID GUNFIRE]

650
00:27:35,067 --> 00:27:37,433
<i>So you're married now, Gabo.
I wish you had told us.</i>

651
00:27:37,567 --> 00:27:38,433
<i> She's pretty.</i>

652
00:27:38,567 --> 00:27:39,633
<i> Since when did I get here?</i>

653
00:27:39,767 --> 00:27:40,800
<i> You just arrived last night.</i>

654
00:27:40,933 --> 00:27:42,933
<i>I was actually surprised
about your coming here.</i>

655
00:27:43,067 --> 00:27:44,000
I didn't know you got released.

656
00:27:44,133 --> 00:27:45,367
<i>Why? What were
the charges against me?</i>

657
00:27:45,500 --> 00:27:47,900
Fraud! And didn't you kill those
<i> who were collecting from you?</i>

658
00:27:48,033 --> 00:27:49,033
<i> Murder?</i>

659
00:27:49,333 --> 00:27:51,100
<i>I promised that
once you were free</i>

660
00:27:51,500 --> 00:27:53,067
<i> and we were finally together,</i>

661
00:27:53,500 --> 00:27:58,033
<i>I'd care for you
and love you endlessly.</i>

662
00:27:58,167 --> 00:28:00,200
<i> Gloria, I love you so much.</i>

663
00:28:00,333 --> 00:28:01,433
<i> You're my beloved.</i>
